    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0453" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1596</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.50 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2830. Your 2118, September 15, 5 p. m. Foreign Office informs me that
                    arrangements referred to in your telegram have not been perfected but that
                    negotiations are at present taking place. Under arrangement with British
                    Government, Swedish Cotton Spinner Association accepts 10,000 bales of cotton a
                    month.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
